# Xcode build products and derived data. `install-on-device.sh` and the build
# commands write these here rather than into ~/Library, so they must not be
# committed — they are hundreds of megabytes and rebuild from source.
build/
build-*/
DerivedData/
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/

# xcodegen writes the project from project.yml; the .xcodeproj is a build
# product, not a source file.
Florin.xcodeproj/
# Except the shared scheme. Xcode Cloud clones this repository and builds a
# scheme it finds in xcshareddata — it does not run xcodegen, so a scheme that
# only exists after generation is a scheme it can never select. This one file
# is the exception that lets a hosted build know what to build.
!Florin.xcodeproj/
Florin.xcodeproj/*
!Florin.xcodeproj/xcshareddata/
!Florin.xcodeproj/xcshareddata/**
